response_schema:
Response schema v1 (strict JSON, no duplicate keys or unknown fields):
{"reconstruction":[{"id":"original assertion id","subject":"entity id","predicate":"relation id","object":{"type":"entity|text|boolean|integer","value":"correctly typed value"},"times":{"event_ms":null,"record_ms":0,"interpretation_ms":0},"provenance":{"asserted_by":"entity id","method":"observed|reported|inferred","evidence":["evidence id"]},"uncertainty":{"kind":"unknown"}}],"comprehension":{"question id":"exact JSON answer"},"application":{"question id":"exact JSON answer"}}
For known confidence use {"kind":"confidence","permille":0..1000}. Use integers for all times (UTC epoch milliseconds); unknown event_ms must be explicit null. Preserve all original ids, each conflicting assertion and its metadata. Reconstruction order is immaterial. Evidence references are a set without duplicates. Missing reconstruction fields lose their category points; missing assertion ids count omissions. Extra assertion ids count inventions. Repeated ids are malformed. Answers use the exact JSON scalar/array type requested by each question; array order matters. Missing answer keys are omissions, additional keys inventions, wrong values errors. Do not include reasoning, extra fields, or markdown. This is an exact structured rubric, not free-form semantic evaluation.
